//api.github.com/users/breskeby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breskeby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/breskeby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The test `NodeShutdownIT.testCRUD` failures (see https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/72787) do not include repro lines with the failures.\r\n\r\nExample build scans: [One](https://gradle-enterprise.elastic.co/s/zzvdmnhxpoudm/tests/:x-pack:plugin:shutdown:qa:multi-node:javaRestTest/org.elasticsearch.xpack.shutdown.NodeShutdownIT/testCRUD?top-execution=1), [Two](https://gradle-enterprise.elastic.co/s/gy32ik4jax3ua/tests/:x-pack:plugin:shutdown:qa:multi-node:javaRestTest/org.elasticsearch.xpack.shutdown.NodeShutdownIT/testCRUD?top-execution=1)\r\n\r\nThis appears to happen reliably with this test.\r\n\r\nPR https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/72772 should fix the test failures, which occur because the other test in `NodeShutdownIT`, `testAllocationPreventedForRemoval`, does not remove the node shutdown it registers, which leaks into `testCRUD` and causes assumptions to fail. The failure will occur any time `testAllocationPreventedForRemoval` runs before `testCRUD`. A repro line that appears to reproduce this reliably is:\r\n```\r\n./gradlew ':x-pack:plugin:shutdown:qa:multi-node:javaRestTest' --tests \"org.elasticsearch.xpack.shutdown.NodeShutdownIT\" -Dtests.seed=91EA8B18627FA3AA -Dtests.locale=ja -Dtests.timezone=America/Louisville\r\n```\r\n\r\nAt some point, that repro line came from a `testCRUD` failure (it's been edited to run all of `NodeShutdownIT`), but I think it was a local failure? I've unfortunately lost my terminal history back that far.","closed_